# NEWCONDO PROPERTY MARKING SERVICE POLICY

**Effective Date:** October 14, 2025  
**Last Updated:** October 14, 2025

---

## 1. INTRODUCTION

This Property Marking Service Policy ("Policy") governs the use of Newcondo's property marking services, which enable property owners and authorized agents to mark and verify property boundaries on our platform through geolocation mapping and boundary verification.

By using Newcondo's Property Marking Service, you agree to comply with this Policy, our Terms of Service, and all applicable laws and regulations.

---

## 2. SERVICE OVERVIEW

### 2.1 Purpose
The Property Marking Service is designed to:
- Verify property geolocation and boundaries
- Prevent duplicate property listings
- Create a transparent property database
- Protect property owners' rights
- Enable accurate property representation

### 2.2 Marking Methods
Property owners may mark their properties through:
1. **Self-Marking:** Mark the property yourself using our mapping interface
2. **Known Contact Marking:** Share a secure link with someone you trust to mark on your behalf
3. **Newcondo Agent Assignment:** Assign the job to verified Newcondo agents in your area
4. **Newcondo Admin Service:** Request Newcondo's admin team to mark the property

---

## 3. ELIGIBILITY

### 3.1 Who Can Request Marking Services
- Property owners with verified accounts
- Authorized property agents with valid agency agreements
- Property managers with proper authorization

### 3.2 Who Can Perform Marking Jobs
- Premium plan subscribers (Renters)
- Verified Newcondo agents
- Newcondo admin team
- Authorized contacts designated by property owners

### 3.3 Account Requirements
- Completed identity verification
- Virtual account creation
- Active account in good standing
- Compliance with platform policies

---

## 4. MARKING PROCESS

### 4.1 Property Boundary Marking
- Properties must be marked using satellite map view
- Boundaries must accurately represent the physical property
- Masks must not overlap with existing marked properties
- GPS coordinates are automatically captured
- Markers must draw accurate boundary polygons

### 4.2 Required Information
Property owners must provide:
- Complete property address (State, LGA, City, Location)
- Contact person details for property access
- Access instructions and preferred timing
- Property images (if available)
- Proof of ownership or authorization

### 4.3 Marking Verification Process
1. Marker draws property boundary on satellite map
2. Marker uploads verification photos (key areas and rooms)
3. Property owner receives notification
4. Owner reviews and confirms marking within 2-3 days
5. Upon confirmation, property is validated for listing

---

## 5. PRICING AND PAYMENT

### 5.1 Service Fees
- **Self-Marking:** Free
- **Known Contact Marking:** Free
- **Agent Marking:** ₦20,000 per property
- **Newcondo Admin Marking:** ₦25,000 per property

### 5.2 Payment Terms
- Payment must be made before job assignment
- Fees are processed through secure virtual accounts
- Agent compensation: 25% of marking fee (₦5,000)
- Platform fee: 75% of marking fee (₦15,000)
- Partial payments released based on completion milestones

### 5.3 Refund Policy
- Full refund if no agent accepts within 48 hours
- Partial refund if marking is incomplete after maximum attempts
- No refund after successful marking confirmation
- Disputed markings handled through admin review

---

## 6. AGENT RESPONSIBILITIES

### 6.1 Service Standards
Agents must:
- Respond to assignments within 3-hour time window
- Visit property at scheduled time
- Take clear, comprehensive property photos
- Mark accurate property boundaries
- Upload verification photos promptly
- Maintain professional conduct
- Protect property owner privacy

### 6.2 Photo Requirements
Agents must capture:
- Property exterior from multiple angles
- Main entrance and access points
- Key rooms (living area, bedrooms, kitchen, bathrooms)
- Unique identifying features
- Building context and surroundings
- Minimum 8-10 clear photos

### 6.3 Prohibited Actions
Agents must not:
- Share property owner information
- Enter property without permission
- Mark properties inaccurately
- Accept bribes or side payments
- List properties without owner consent
- Disclose property details to third parties

---

## 7. PROPERTY OWNER RESPONSIBILITIES

### 7.1 Information Accuracy
Property owners must:
- Provide accurate property information
- Ensure legal right to list property
- Provide valid contact information
- Grant necessary access for marking
- Respond to confirmation requests promptly

### 7.2 Confirmation Timeline
- **Initial Confirmation Window:** 2-3 days from marking completion
- **Consequences of Non-Confirmation:**
  - After deadline: Partial agent compensation released
  - After X failed confirmations: Full fee paid to agent
  - Property owner must initiate new marking job

### 7.3 Marking Rejection
Property owners may reject marking if:
- Boundary marking is inaccurate
- Photos do not match property
- Wrong property was marked
- Quality standards not met

---

## 8. TIME WINDOWS AND DEADLINES

### 8.1 Agent Response Time
- 3-hour maximum window per agent
- First-come, first-served queue system
- Auto-advance to next agent if time expires

### 8.2 Marking Completion
- Agent has 3 hours from acceptance to complete marking
- Partial payment (₦1,000) released upon completion
- Remainder held pending owner confirmation

### 8.3 Owner Confirmation
- 2-3 days from marking completion
- Automatic escalation if deadline missed
- Multiple notification attempts

---

## 9. QUALITY ASSURANCE

### 9.1 Duplicate Prevention
- System automatically detects overlapping boundaries
- Red-gray transparent overlay indicates marked properties
- Prevents multiple listings of same property
- Building fingerprint verification

### 9.2 Boundary Validation
- Maximum property size limits enforced
- Overlapping boundaries rejected
- GPS coordinate verification
- Admin review for disputed boundaries

### 9.3 Agent Performance Tracking
- Reliability score maintained (0-5.00)
- Completion rate monitoring
- User feedback incorporation
- Suspension for repeated violations

---

## 10. DISPUTE RESOLUTION

### 10.1 Boundary Disputes
- Report through platform interface
- Admin review within 3-5 business days
- Evidence submission by both parties
- Final decision by Newcondo admin team

### 10.2 Service Quality Issues
- Property owner can reject substandard marking
- Agent compensation withheld pending review
- Admin mediation available
- Refund consideration on case-by-case basis

### 10.3 Payment Disputes
- Virtual account transaction records reviewed
- Payment holds for disputed transactions
- Resolution timeline: 5-7 business days
- Appeal process available

---

## 11. DATA AND PRIVACY

### 11.1 Location Data
- GPS coordinates collected and stored
- Boundary data associated with property
- Used only for platform purposes
- Protected under our Privacy Policy

### 11.2 Photo Storage
- Verification photos stored securely
- Used for property verification and display
- Property owner retains image rights
- Third-party access restricted

### 11.3 Contact Information
- Shared only with assigned markers
- Used solely for marking coordination
- Deleted after job completion
- Never sold or shared with marketers

---

## 12. SERVICE SUSPENSION AND TERMINATION

### 12.1 Grounds for Suspension
Newcondo may suspend marking services for:
- Fraudulent property information
- Repeated marking violations
- Abuse of agent services
- Non-payment of fees
- Platform policy violations

### 12.2 Agent Deactivation
Agents may be deactivated for:
- Low reliability scores (below 3.00)
- Multiple completion failures
- Inappropriate conduct
- Privacy violations
- Falsified marking information

